{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Esau was forty years old, and he took as wife Judith the daughter of Beeri the Hittite, and Basemath.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: all forty years Esau would hunt women, violating them; and when he reached forty years he likened himself to his father, saying: my father married a wife at forty, so I too am forty. And Asaph spoke of his nation (Psalms 80:14): ״יכרסמנה חזיר מיער״ — the boar from the forest gnaws it; and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: just as the pig displays its hooves and says, 'See, I am pure,' so too the children of Esau rob and plunder and present themselves as if they are servants of the blessed Name; and Esau's wives were Hittite women, and the Hittite is among the seven nations whom Israel were commanded to put under the ban, as it is said (Deuteronomy 20:17): ״כי החרם תחרימם החתי האמורי וגו״ — but you shall utterly put them under the ban, the Hittite, the Amorite, etc. And Scripture declared that Esau the wicked took his wives from the seed of the wicked, and this is what is written (Psalms 125:5): ״והמטים עקלקלותם יוליכם ה' את פועלי האון״ — and those who turn aside to their crooked ways, may YHWH lead them away with the workers of iniquity; that is to say, they join themselves to the workers of iniquity — and then peace upon Israel, that no unfit seed will mingle with their seed. See how Esau went after his own kind; and our Rabbis of blessed memory said: not for naught did the starling go with the raven, but because it is of his kind — let this one come from the bosom of this one, and be turned aside to the embrace of this one."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The Aramaic proverb at the end (ייתי הדין מחיק שמא ויסב להדין מחיקת שמא) is rendered hyper-literally; the repeated דין/שמא pun resists smooth English. The citation תהילים פ׳:י״ד (Psalms 80:14) is rendered as written; verse reference reflects chapter 80 in the Hebrew numbering."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:28.344506599Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}